546499d1`, trailer `WI: WI-852`) records `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2` and `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=2`, and the pre-commit hook passed.\n\n**Amendment: both rows changed meaning.**\n- **SR-146 is blessed.** It now also covers review and critique briefs rendered by an attended launcher, and adds that a refused render writes no brief. Its per-session record is limited to loop sessions. The new clause is verified: `test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written` runs the command line and asserts no output file exists.\n- **SR-154 is not blessed.** Its acceptance criteria gained a clause about recording an attended review verdict, but its Requirement still begins \"When unattended work reaches integration…\". The acceptance now tests something the requirement doesn't ask for. The fix is either to widen the Requirement or to move the clause to SR-146, which this same change set already widened.\n\n**First approval: LLR-313 and TC-333 are returned.** Besides SR-154 being unsettled, these clauses have no test behind them:\n- `lane_commits` and IF-289's three git refusals (not on a branch, not a commit, base not an ancestor) are never called; the one command-line test monkeypatches `lane_commits` out.\n- No test drives exit 0, the success code, for either the `review` or `file` command.\n- No test covers an empty test list, an empty named input, a missing findings file, or the critique render with a missing spec.\n\nThe current tests pass (`14 passed`).\n\n**Re-attestation refused.** I ran `snapshot --reattests SR-146` and it refused, naming SR-154's drifted `AcceptanceCriteria` in the same registry. As the brief instructs, I did not add SR-154 (which I didn't bless) to the call. SR-146 stays unanchored until SR-154 is settled, so the coordinator should put both in the same next sitting. There is no act commit, and the tree is clean apart from the `.requested` marker.\n\n**The follow-up:** I drafted one item in WI-852's spec `## Dispositions`, and the intake parser reads it