e is driven.\n3. Bring LLR-313 and TC-333 back for first approval in the same sitting as SR-154's re-attestation. IF-288 and IF-289, which TC-333 claims to verify, will rest on the same evidence.\n\nObservation, not a ruling: `review_brief.py`'s docstring says a narrow round's `-narrow` suffix means it \"never reads as the full-lane review a landing needs\". But `kitlib.verdict.ROUND_FILE_RE` reads the suffix as an ordinary tag, and nothing in `score_reviews` or `integrate` distinguishes it. That is the lane reviewer's to check, not part of the rows above.\nEOF\npython -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,'project-trajectory/scripts'); import intake\nt=open(r'''$f''',encoding='utf-8').read(); d,r=intake.parse_dispositions(t,'WI-852'); print(r,[x['title'][:50] for x in d])\"\ngit add docs/reviews/wi-852-coordinator-renders-kit-briefs/001-ADJUDICATE-d75fdc2.md \"$f\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' > /dev/null 2>&1; echo exit=$?; git log --oneline -1; git show --stat HEAD | tail -3\nreview: WI-852 adjudication at d75fdc2: amendment MEANING (SR-146 blessed, SR-154 not), first-approval RETURN (LLR-313, TC-333)\n\nCombined sitting (amendment;first-approval). SR-146 widens to attended\nrenders and adds the no-brief-on-refusal clause; it is blessed, and the\nclause is verified by the unfilled-slot command-line test. SR-154 adds an\nattended-recording acceptance clause that its unchanged Requirement\n(\"when unattended work reaches integration\") cannot carry, so it is not\nblessed. LLR-313 and TC-333 go back: lane_commits and IF-289's git\nrefusals are never driven (monkeypatched out), and the empty-test-list,\nempty-input and critique-missing-spec clauses have no verifying case.\nOne follow-up is drafted in the spec's ## Dispositions.\n\nWI: WI-852\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF","is_backgrounded":false,"task_type":"local_bash","uuid":"fe9d9e2a-6d6f-498d-bdc2-e2bfd477dc7f","session_id":"b8cf33a7-067d-4b49-9e30-523229883c86"}
